WEBVTT

00:36.828 --> 00:38.663
Checkmate.

00:41.291 --> 00:44.210
Oh! That's the legendary hitman for you!

00:44.294 --> 00:46.671
You're saying that on purpose.

00:46.755 --> 00:49.048
It's been a while
since you let me take you on,

00:49.132 --> 00:51.593
but even as a middle schooler,
your strength is seriously cracked!

00:51.676 --> 00:55.472
Well, I've definitely lost
some strength now that I'm younger.

00:55.555 --> 00:58.892
On the other hand, since I still have
all my experience and knowledge,

00:58.975 --> 01:01.561
maybe I can actually move better
in the field than I used to.

01:01.644 --> 01:04.522
Were you actually human in your prime?

01:05.440 --> 01:06.274
I mean...

01:06.357 --> 01:09.444
I did get a fresh reminder that
you've always been freakishly strong

01:09.527 --> 01:11.738
even back in middle school...

01:11.821 --> 01:16.326
But still, do not go all out without
thinking about the consequences again

01:16.409 --> 01:18.161
like you did with Tenma!

01:18.244 --> 01:22.123
Seriously, I'm pretty sure the kids
from Home Ec are still suspicious!

01:22.207 --> 01:23.875
Yeah, yeah. I get it.

01:24.459 --> 01:28.129
And apparently, the report I sent
the Boss still wasn't detailed enough.

01:28.213 --> 01:31.883
How damn thorough does
that doting father need to be?

01:31.966 --> 01:34.677
Listen, okay? If you're gonna keep
living as a middle schooler,

01:34.761 --> 01:37.138
the one rule is never let anyone
find out who you really are.

01:37.722 --> 01:39.182
For the Boss's mission.

01:39.265 --> 01:40.767
For your paycheck.

01:41.267 --> 01:42.393
And more than anything...

01:42.977 --> 01:44.854
for your own sake, Boss.

01:45.939 --> 01:48.566
At least, that's how
I've been seeing it lately.

01:50.652 --> 01:51.486
Yeah.

01:52.362 --> 01:53.822
You're right.

03:24.996 --> 03:27.457
HOME EC ROOM

03:27.540 --> 03:28.416
Ogami...

03:28.499 --> 03:29.751
Noren...

03:30.293 --> 03:31.794
I have a favor to ask.

03:31.878 --> 03:33.046
This weekend...

03:33.630 --> 03:36.799
would you two go on a double date with me?

03:39.677 --> 03:40.553
Huh?

03:40.637 --> 03:41.471
What?!

03:41.554 --> 03:44.557
President, don't tell me
you decided to go out with Tenma!

03:44.641 --> 03:47.268
I-I didn't! I have
no intention of doing that!

03:48.019 --> 03:49.062
But...

03:50.313 --> 03:51.439
I love you!

03:52.523 --> 03:53.358
I love you!

03:53.441 --> 03:54.359
Huh?

03:55.193 --> 03:56.361
Chisato!

03:58.238 --> 04:01.699
He's been showing up every single day,
and I sort of let it slip...

04:01.783 --> 04:04.077
that maybe I could
at least go on one date.

04:04.160 --> 04:05.828
Wow, you fold way easier than I thought!

04:05.912 --> 04:08.373
I mean, a double date?

04:08.456 --> 04:09.540
- Why?
- Yeah.

04:09.624 --> 04:14.337
I said, "Two of us alone is impossible,
but if Noren and Oga come, then okay."

04:14.420 --> 04:16.089
No, do not drag us into this!

04:16.172 --> 04:17.590
You're usually so on top of things,

04:17.674 --> 04:20.051
but when it comes to this stuff,
you're hopeless.

04:20.134 --> 04:22.053
Yeah, I'm ashamed to admit it.

04:22.136 --> 04:24.180
Get it together! Keep this up...

04:24.806 --> 04:27.558
and someday you're gonna be
one of those businesswomen

04:27.642 --> 04:31.437
who scare off every guy around her
because they're too competent at work.

04:31.521 --> 04:32.480
Chisato!

04:32.563 --> 04:34.399
And then get suckered
by some random pushy loser!

04:34.482 --> 04:37.986
I just thought maybe if I went on
one date with him, he'd be satisfied.

04:38.069 --> 04:39.487
What kind of a plan is that?

04:39.570 --> 04:43.157
It's even more delusional than
Japan's low birthrate countermeasures!

04:45.285 --> 04:49.205
SATURDAY, MAY 23RD

04:50.248 --> 04:51.749
Somehow...

04:51.833 --> 04:54.502
I ended up getting
roped into this double date.

04:55.086 --> 04:58.881
But honestly, I'm still curious
about Ogami's secret.

04:58.965 --> 05:02.260
Maybe I'll find out something today.

05:02.343 --> 05:03.469
Yo!

05:03.553 --> 05:04.637
President!

05:04.721 --> 05:07.223
Man, I'm really sorry about all this.

05:07.307 --> 05:09.100
Wait, what is that outfit?

05:09.183 --> 05:13.313
Oh, well, with the duel thing, this is
sort of anti-pickup-guy protection.

05:13.396 --> 05:15.398
Oh, you're already here!

05:15.481 --> 05:16.733
Sorry to keep you waiting!

05:16.816 --> 05:19.110
- That's workout gear!
- Huh?

05:19.193 --> 05:21.946
I wasn't expecting you
to show up stylish or anything...

05:22.030 --> 05:23.906
But come on! That's workout gear!

05:23.990 --> 05:25.033
Huh? Is it bad?

05:25.116 --> 05:27.869
You know this is a date, right?
Not the gym?

05:28.453 --> 05:32.874
Who the hell said Unicorns
were perfect inside and out?

05:32.957 --> 05:35.418
His stats are ridiculously lopsided.

05:35.501 --> 05:38.337
In fact, everything
got dumped into physical.

05:38.421 --> 05:40.923
A date with my beloved Chisato!

05:41.007 --> 05:42.550
I'm so, so happy!

05:44.218 --> 05:45.470
But he's so pure!

05:45.553 --> 05:48.139
At this rate,
he's just gonna steamroll you!

05:48.222 --> 05:49.974
Huh? Am I last?

05:50.058 --> 05:51.893
Sorry. Kept you waiting.

05:53.978 --> 05:55.063
A jacket and...

05:55.688 --> 05:57.607
- A clutch bag?
- Huh?

05:57.690 --> 05:59.275
This isn't about
whether it's stylish or not!

05:59.358 --> 06:01.110
You're on some completely
different wavelength!

06:01.194 --> 06:03.279
I'm pretty sure I got the size right.

06:04.280 --> 06:05.907
That's not the problem!

06:05.990 --> 06:07.325
A date?

06:07.408 --> 06:08.910
Are you sure about this?

06:09.660 --> 06:11.496
You're an old man, remember?

06:11.579 --> 06:13.164
What choice do I have?

06:13.247 --> 06:16.542
If we're just walking around town,
I'll manage somehow.

06:16.626 --> 06:19.462
I won't be around
when you head out, though.

06:19.545 --> 06:21.130
What are you gonna wear?

06:21.214 --> 06:22.757
It'll be fine.

06:22.840 --> 06:25.426
I'll just wear something normal.

06:26.010 --> 06:28.471
Your "normal" is an automatic fail, Boss!

06:30.181 --> 06:31.349
Still...

06:31.432 --> 06:33.851
what a weird group.

06:33.935 --> 06:37.897
And Noren's outfit is like some celebrity
trying not to be recognized.

06:37.980 --> 06:41.359
Am I the only normal middle schooler here?

06:46.531 --> 06:47.615
Uh...

06:47.698 --> 06:50.118
So, what are we going to do?

06:50.201 --> 06:54.747
I figured we'd browse some shops
around here, then maybe catch a movie.

06:54.831 --> 06:56.499
That's surprisingly normal!

06:56.582 --> 06:58.668
Thank goodness it's not training.

06:59.252 --> 07:02.672
Man, this used to be just
some nothing park back in the day.

07:02.755 --> 07:04.799
There were even homeless guys
hanging around.

07:04.882 --> 07:06.342
Huh? Back in the day?

07:07.510 --> 07:12.223
I mean, I just happened to see
some random old guy write that online!

07:12.306 --> 07:14.183
Don't let your guard down, Boss!

07:15.268 --> 07:16.602
Old guy?

07:18.980 --> 07:23.234
Oh! I've been kind of curious
about that ramen place!

07:23.317 --> 07:25.611
Huh? You like ramen?

07:25.695 --> 07:27.530
What? No...

07:27.613 --> 07:30.158
I mean... I have it
once in a while, I guess!

07:30.241 --> 07:34.120
That place has a line full
of seriously hardcore customers.

07:34.203 --> 07:35.830
You wanna go heavy, huh?

07:35.913 --> 07:37.707
Sorry, ramen's out for me.

07:37.790 --> 07:39.584
Today's not a cheat day.

07:39.667 --> 07:41.711
You're seriously training at that level?

07:43.421 --> 07:46.299
Well, I guess
I am getting a little hungry.

07:47.300 --> 07:49.177
Wanna duck into
that coffee house over there?

07:49.260 --> 07:50.386
"Coffee house"?

07:50.470 --> 07:53.014
I mean, it's not like nobody says that...

07:53.097 --> 07:56.225
but when Ogami says it,
it fits way too well!

08:11.949 --> 08:13.618
Man...

08:13.701 --> 08:15.870
this has been fun, Chisato!

08:15.953 --> 08:17.580
O-Oh yeah?

08:17.663 --> 08:20.833
Crap. Somehow
I actually had a pretty good time.

08:25.880 --> 08:27.048
I knew it!

08:27.131 --> 08:30.635
I thought so before, too,
but it's not so much that he's weird!

08:30.718 --> 08:32.220
It's like he's a totally different age!

08:32.303 --> 08:34.305
But plain and simple,
he's a middle schooler for sure!

08:34.388 --> 08:36.390
It's not like he just looks young!

08:38.351 --> 08:39.769
Oh, shit!

08:50.154 --> 08:52.365
What the hell? My body is suddenly...

09:02.208 --> 09:05.211
Crap! Did I pass out?

09:05.294 --> 09:07.838
Judging by the scene,
has it been about an hour?

09:09.507 --> 09:11.759
Huh? My hands look old.

09:13.052 --> 09:15.346
Wait... this stubble...

09:16.305 --> 09:19.475
What?! I'm back to being an adult?

09:20.059 --> 09:21.394
Was there some trigger?

09:21.477 --> 09:24.272
Or did the wasp venom
just wear off naturally?

09:24.355 --> 09:26.274
No, that doesn't matter right now!

09:26.357 --> 09:27.775
This is really bad!

09:27.858 --> 09:29.527
By "bad," I mean...

09:30.528 --> 09:33.322
The visuals! Why now?

09:33.406 --> 09:37.201
Could the timing possibly be
any worse? If they...

09:37.827 --> 09:39.453
notice me like this...

09:39.537 --> 09:41.872
- EEK
- AH!

09:41.956 --> 09:44.458
Oh, no. I already want to die.

09:45.918 --> 09:48.004
Ogami, is something wrong?

09:48.504 --> 09:49.630
Bathroom!

09:49.714 --> 09:50.673
Huh?

09:55.678 --> 09:59.432
Now that I'm thinking clearly,
what the hell am I doing?

10:00.224 --> 10:03.311
Even if I felt more
like a chaperone tagging along,

10:03.394 --> 10:06.272
what kind of grown-ass man goes
on a double date with middle schoolers?

10:06.355 --> 10:07.523
Am I an idiot?

10:08.107 --> 10:10.359
That snapped me right back to my senses.

10:10.443 --> 10:13.112
I panicked a little,
but I'm back to normal now.

10:13.195 --> 10:14.989
This little game ends here.

10:15.072 --> 10:16.782
I'm just gonna bail.

10:16.866 --> 10:21.287
I do feel a little bad
about breaking my promise to Noren...

10:21.871 --> 10:24.957
but an old guy going to middle school
in the first place is insane.

10:25.458 --> 10:26.876
Hey, Ogami!

10:26.959 --> 10:29.128
- Huh? Tenma?
- What, did you fall in?

10:29.211 --> 10:30.588
The movie's over--

10:31.714 --> 10:32.882
That scared me.

10:32.965 --> 10:33.758
Hey!

10:33.841 --> 10:36.344
Coming all the way over to the stall?
Of course he would!

10:36.969 --> 10:39.305
Dammit, what do I do?

10:42.183 --> 10:44.060
Oh, we're connected.

10:44.560 --> 10:45.895
What happened?

10:46.562 --> 10:48.481
Don't say anything! Just look at this!

10:49.982 --> 10:51.025
Y-You're back!

10:51.108 --> 10:55.279
And Noren and the others are outside
so I can't get out of this damn restroom.

10:55.363 --> 10:59.325
All you brought today
was that clutch bag, right?

10:59.408 --> 11:02.912
Lock picks, mini bombs
and a bunch of useless...

11:02.995 --> 11:03.829
Oh!

11:03.913 --> 11:06.832
The cat-shaped voice-changer sticker!

11:06.916 --> 11:09.168
At least it's not a bow tie.

11:09.251 --> 11:11.462
Hey, are you really okay in there?

11:12.046 --> 11:13.964
Stick it around your Adam's apple.

11:14.548 --> 11:17.843
Then use the app on your phone
to change the frequency, and...

11:18.511 --> 11:19.553
U-Uh...

11:19.637 --> 11:22.681
I-I might not be okay.

11:22.765 --> 11:24.141
Huh? Seriously?

11:24.767 --> 11:27.395
M-My stomach's messed up.
I can't come out.

11:27.478 --> 11:29.563
You three go home without me.

11:29.647 --> 11:32.191
It's that bad? Should I call an ambulance?

11:32.274 --> 11:36.153
No! It's not that bad!
But I can't come out right away!

11:36.237 --> 11:39.156
We were only heading home anyway,
so just go! Please!

11:40.282 --> 11:41.867
Okay.

11:41.951 --> 11:43.327
I'll tell them.

11:43.411 --> 11:45.121
Oh, thank goodness!

11:45.204 --> 11:48.374
Now if I just wait a little and come out,
I can get home safe, and--

11:48.457 --> 11:49.750
W-Who are...

11:49.834 --> 11:51.585
W-What the...

11:51.669 --> 11:53.170
- Hey! Wait! Tenma!
- Huh?

11:53.254 --> 11:55.172
- Ogami! Noren just...
- Safety...

11:55.256 --> 11:56.841
Is officially off the table?

11:56.924 --> 11:58.384
Noren got kidnapped!

11:58.467 --> 12:00.386
Another kidnapping?

12:00.469 --> 12:01.929
Again with this crap?

12:02.012 --> 12:06.183
Noren, even this old man's
starting to feel sorry for you!

12:06.767 --> 12:08.060
Dammit! No, I can't!

12:08.144 --> 12:09.603
I can't just leave her!

12:09.687 --> 12:11.730
If I go home now,
I'll never sleep right again!

12:11.814 --> 12:13.149
Dammit!

12:13.732 --> 12:14.525
You okay?

12:14.608 --> 12:16.026
I'm fine.

12:16.110 --> 12:17.528
But Noren...

12:17.611 --> 12:20.906
Boss! If you come out like that,
they're gonna get a good look at you!

12:20.990 --> 12:23.826
Tenma!
Hug her as hard as you can! Right now!

12:23.909 --> 12:24.952
Huh?

12:25.035 --> 12:25.911
Huh?

12:27.329 --> 12:28.581
Like this?

12:29.790 --> 12:32.209
Big Sis!
What did the kidnappers look like?

12:33.461 --> 12:35.629
Uh, there were two of them!

12:35.713 --> 12:38.048
Both wearing black hoodies!

12:41.177 --> 12:43.304
A black van! Heading toward Gaien?

12:48.100 --> 12:49.268
TENGOKU / GAIENZAKA

12:49.351 --> 12:50.978
Huh? Hey, wait!

12:51.061 --> 12:52.897
Message this number!

12:54.273 --> 12:55.441
I'll pay you!

12:56.525 --> 12:58.152
What?!

12:58.235 --> 13:01.405
Dammit! One thing after another!

13:06.994 --> 13:09.121
Boss, I just realized something.

13:09.205 --> 13:10.164
Yeah?

13:10.247 --> 13:11.749
That whole restroom thing...

13:11.832 --> 13:14.752
Couldn't you have just walked out
pretending to be a total stranger?

13:14.835 --> 13:16.545
Oh! Yeah!

13:16.629 --> 13:18.631
I panicked and didn't think of it!

13:19.798 --> 13:21.759
Well, that's rare.

13:22.343 --> 13:24.595
He's been in plenty
of situations that called for

13:24.678 --> 13:26.680
way tougher split-second calls than that.

13:26.764 --> 13:30.226
And him panicking over
anything at all is out of character.

13:30.309 --> 13:33.229
Was he really enjoying
middle school life that much?

13:35.481 --> 13:37.733
Jeez! How long
are you gonna keep hugging me?

13:37.816 --> 13:39.944
Oh. I was so happy, I forgot.

13:40.027 --> 13:41.946
This is not the time!

13:42.029 --> 13:46.367
Ogami went after them alone,
and I don't know what we can even do...

13:46.450 --> 13:47.826
But we have to go after him!

13:47.910 --> 13:48.744
Huh?

13:48.827 --> 13:49.995
Why?

13:51.997 --> 13:55.125
As long as you're safe, I'm good, Chisato.

13:55.209 --> 13:56.794
Do I have to go?

13:56.877 --> 13:58.671
Ogami already went, didn't he?

14:03.425 --> 14:04.593
Well...

14:05.261 --> 14:07.137
of course you do!

14:07.221 --> 14:09.098
What are you, a robot?

14:09.181 --> 14:11.976
Did you already forget
what we talked about?

14:12.059 --> 14:14.478
When someone's in trouble,
you help each other!

14:14.562 --> 14:18.649
Sure, we're middle schoolers!
I know encouraging us to go is crazy!

14:19.233 --> 14:21.610
But that attitude is not okay!

14:21.694 --> 14:24.655
And here I was,
actually having a little fun today!

14:24.738 --> 14:26.740
Don't make me lose respect for you!

14:26.824 --> 14:29.076
Someone who talks
like that at a time like this...

14:29.159 --> 14:31.328
I could never like him!

14:35.416 --> 14:36.792
I'm sorry.

14:36.876 --> 14:39.420
People have always told me
I can't read the room

14:39.503 --> 14:42.047
or that I don't understand
how other people feel.

14:42.882 --> 14:45.843
Even when I think I get it,
I don't really get it.

14:47.136 --> 14:49.054
And I'm sure
that's going to keep happening.

14:49.138 --> 14:50.139
So...

14:51.015 --> 14:52.474
I want you to teach me.

14:53.142 --> 14:54.518
I'll try.

14:54.602 --> 14:56.729
So I don't make you cry, Chisato.

14:57.980 --> 14:59.023
Okay!

14:59.106 --> 15:00.149
I'm going.

15:00.774 --> 15:03.277
Chisato, stay here and call the police.

15:03.360 --> 15:04.945
No, I'm going, too--

15:05.029 --> 15:07.740
You're slow, and you'd probably
just get in the way.

15:08.282 --> 15:10.743
- Hello? Ogami? Where are you right now?
- Ten seconds ago...

15:10.826 --> 15:12.828
You said you were going
to try not to make me cry!

15:16.832 --> 15:18.208
Jeez, Tenma...

15:18.292 --> 15:20.085
He's coming, too?

15:20.169 --> 15:22.338
And what the hell is this crap?

15:22.421 --> 15:26.467
Can't believe I turned back into a kid
again in the middle of chasing them.

15:26.550 --> 15:28.052
Okay, I'm here!

15:28.677 --> 15:29.720
Sorry to keep you waiting!

15:29.803 --> 15:32.014
That was fast! How'd you get here?

15:32.097 --> 15:33.933
Huh? I ran.

15:34.016 --> 15:35.726
It was only two or three kilometers.

15:35.809 --> 15:39.146
He's not a triple threat
Superman for nothing.

15:44.526 --> 15:45.611
There they are.

15:47.196 --> 15:48.614
Those guys...

15:48.697 --> 15:52.117
They don't feel
like your average NPCs, do they?

15:52.201 --> 15:54.078
Are they high or something?

15:54.161 --> 15:55.245
Yeah.

15:55.329 --> 15:57.164
Crap! I screwed up!

15:57.247 --> 16:00.751
I figured they were just low-level thugs,
so I brought Tenma along...

16:00.834 --> 16:02.252
But that mark...

16:02.336 --> 16:04.254
Their organization's bigger than ours.

16:04.838 --> 16:09.551
In number of assassins, track record,
sales, and customer satisfaction...

16:09.635 --> 16:12.846
They're number one across the board!
The biggest name in the business!

16:12.930 --> 16:14.014
JARDIN!

16:14.098 --> 16:17.518
They use a rank system
based on the client's membership fee,

16:17.601 --> 16:21.021
and the higher the rank,
the tougher the assassins they send.

16:21.563 --> 16:26.193
Supposedly, only VIPs are allowed
to join the top-tier Black-Rank!

16:26.276 --> 16:28.821
Huh? There's two of 'em.

16:29.947 --> 16:31.365
The little one is...

16:31.448 --> 16:32.950
Well, whatever.

16:33.033 --> 16:34.827
Kazuma Rindou. Age 15!

16:34.910 --> 16:37.579
Either way, this'll be over in no time.

16:37.663 --> 16:41.250
The big one is Eiji Rindou. Age 13!

16:43.335 --> 16:46.338
They're both Black-Rank assassins!

16:46.422 --> 16:48.757
Hold up! That's a middle schooler?

16:49.591 --> 16:50.426
Huh?

16:53.053 --> 16:54.304
Hello?

16:54.388 --> 16:57.224
Hey, nice to meet you, Ogami.

16:57.307 --> 16:59.476
And Tenma Tendo, as well.

17:01.145 --> 17:02.563
What do you want?

17:02.646 --> 17:06.483
Why, the Mitsuoka duel, of course.
And the position of fiancé.

17:07.067 --> 17:08.027
Though...

17:08.110 --> 17:10.487
I'll formally challenge you
for that another day.

17:10.571 --> 17:12.072
Today, my goal is...

17:12.156 --> 17:13.699
Noren's heart.

17:15.034 --> 17:17.202
My specialty is hypnosis.

17:17.870 --> 17:20.622
I'm going to use it
to make her fall in love with Eiji here.

17:20.706 --> 17:22.499
Huh? You can't just--

17:22.583 --> 17:23.667
I can.

17:24.752 --> 17:29.006
I can hypnotize anyone
powerfully and instantly.

17:29.631 --> 17:32.509
If I win the duel,
I can take the position of fiancé.

17:32.593 --> 17:34.887
But merely having the title
would not satisfy me.

17:35.471 --> 17:37.765
Noren Mitsuoka must become

17:37.848 --> 17:40.642
my little brother Eiji's bride
in body and soul.

17:40.726 --> 17:41.977
Wha...

17:43.479 --> 17:45.814
Um, your brother there...

17:45.898 --> 17:49.193
He's only been going
"Oh" and "Ah" this whole time.

17:49.276 --> 17:52.404
Indeed. My brother is a man of few words.

17:52.488 --> 17:54.782
But once she falls in love with him,
that will be a minor detail.

17:54.865 --> 17:57.618
No, this isn't about a "few words."

17:57.701 --> 17:59.036
It's more like, is he alive?

17:59.119 --> 18:01.205
Even if, for argument's sake,
they did get married,

18:01.288 --> 18:04.917
could he actually make
a marriage work long term?

18:06.794 --> 18:08.545
He moves, therefore he lives.

18:08.629 --> 18:12.174
I won't deny there may be certain areas
where he falls short, but not to worry.

18:12.257 --> 18:15.427
I will support him. And with that,
our conversation is over.

18:15.511 --> 18:16.553
Agreed?

18:16.637 --> 18:18.305
Like hell I do!

18:18.388 --> 18:19.640
What a nuisance.

18:20.599 --> 18:22.684
By the way, Tenma...

18:23.185 --> 18:24.645
- Huh?
- Huh? Me?

18:25.270 --> 18:27.231
I have a proposal.

18:27.314 --> 18:30.359
You only came here because
Chisato Shiraishi told you to, right?

18:30.442 --> 18:32.778
If you leave Ogami behind
and go home right now,

18:32.861 --> 18:35.906
I'll use hypnosis to make
Chisato Shiraishi fall in love with you.

18:35.989 --> 18:40.119
You get what you want, and you avoid
putting yourself in unnecessary danger.

18:40.828 --> 18:41.912
Well?

18:41.995 --> 18:43.163
This guy...

18:43.247 --> 18:45.249
He's done a serious amount of research!

18:45.874 --> 18:47.459
Tenma doesn't really understand emotions.

18:48.460 --> 18:49.461
Don't tell me...

18:54.049 --> 18:55.509
Jeez...

18:55.592 --> 18:58.262
You probably shouldn't have said that.

18:58.345 --> 19:01.306
That's basically
like fixing a match, right?

19:02.266 --> 19:04.226
The way I feel about Chisato

19:04.309 --> 19:07.312
is no different from the three sports
I've devoted my life to.

19:07.396 --> 19:10.482
If I have to win by cheating,
I'd rather lose for real and cry about it.

19:11.483 --> 19:12.734
Tenma...

19:12.818 --> 19:15.362
I mean, I'm definitely gonna win, though!

19:15.445 --> 19:18.323
Big Sis, you've got
one hell of an admirer.

19:18.407 --> 19:19.575
So, honestly...

19:19.658 --> 19:23.328
I was already getting pissed off
from the whole Noren thing at the start.

19:23.412 --> 19:25.289
I don't like you guys.

19:25.914 --> 19:28.667
And I'm not really in the mood
to just let this slide.

19:28.750 --> 19:32.045
So, there you have it. We're done talking.

19:32.129 --> 19:35.174
Give Noren back,
you trash-tier matchmaking brothers.

19:35.257 --> 19:37.801
Negotiations have broken down, then.

19:37.885 --> 19:39.178
Very well.

19:40.512 --> 19:41.555
War it is!

19:42.222 --> 19:43.056
Golf?

19:46.602 --> 19:49.271
- Crap! Dodge, Tenma!
- Huh? Okay!

19:52.649 --> 19:54.067
These guys are nuts!

20:00.032 --> 20:02.701
Ogami! Even I can tell
what's going on here!

20:02.784 --> 20:04.870
If that hits us, we're dead!

20:05.370 --> 20:07.206
Yeah, I'm with you on that one!

20:07.789 --> 20:10.751
For now, get out
into the concourse and find cover!

20:13.587 --> 20:15.797
All right. I'll pursue them.

20:16.381 --> 20:20.594
You keep watch over Noren, and
if you sense them anywhere, snipe them!

20:22.721 --> 20:24.932
Dammit, what the hell are these guys?

20:26.767 --> 20:27.935
This is bad!

20:28.018 --> 20:30.187
Empty-handed, even I might be in trouble!

20:30.270 --> 20:33.690
Boss! Can you get toward Block 320?

20:33.774 --> 20:35.734
I sent a drone loaded with guns your way!

20:35.817 --> 20:37.069
For real? You're a lifesaver!

20:37.152 --> 20:41.782
What's gotten into you, Nekota?
You're absolutely killing it today!

20:44.034 --> 20:45.702
Okay, here it comes! That's it!

20:48.956 --> 20:51.208
I'm not letting you
get your hands on a weapon.

20:52.918 --> 20:55.379
You're in the same
line of work, aren't you?

21:00.467 --> 21:02.302
It fell inside the concourse.

21:02.386 --> 21:03.804
But it's too far away.

21:03.887 --> 21:06.640
And if he can hit a drone
from that position...

21:06.723 --> 21:08.558
I won't have time to go grab it!

21:08.642 --> 21:12.020
So, it ends before I even use
my real weapon.

21:12.104 --> 21:13.480
How anticlimactic!

21:14.273 --> 21:15.357
Boss!

21:17.317 --> 21:21.113
The big guy left on the ground
is the sniper, right?

21:26.785 --> 21:27.786
Wha...

21:39.673 --> 21:41.758
He used the sound to make Eiji snipe it,

21:41.842 --> 21:44.052
so the blast wave
would launch the gun toward him?

21:44.136 --> 21:45.178
Listen.

21:45.846 --> 21:50.183
I basically see Noren as a daughter.

21:50.767 --> 21:52.394
Now imagine you're the dad

21:52.477 --> 21:55.689
and some guy shows up at your house
saying, "Please let me have your daughter!

21:55.772 --> 21:57.107
We're in love!

21:57.190 --> 22:00.819
Because I hypnotized her."

22:06.658 --> 22:09.745
Naturally I'm gonna beat
the shit outta you!
